        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/post-oak-bend-tx",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits on a narrow strip of Farm Road 987 and several intersecting roads just north of Kaufman.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/post-oak-bend-tx",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Post Oak Bend is 3 miles north of Kaufman and 9 miles south of Terrell, right in the heart of Texas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Post_Oak_Bend%2C_Texas",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "It lies in central Kaufman County, a region known for its rolling plains and historic ranching.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Post_Oak_Bend%2C_Texas",
